@layout MainLayout
@page "/tools/share-text"

<ToolsLanding Heading="Share text with a link — no account needed"
              Description="Paste text, get a link. The snippet renders inline for the reader, is encrypted in your browser, and expires on its own."
              Lede="Paste a snippet, send the link. Whoever opens it reads the text on the page — they do not have to download a file."
              PasteHint="Paste your text anywhere on this page">
    <Body>
        <h2 class="db-h2">How it works</h2>
        <p>
            Press Ctrl+V. The text becomes a small <code>.txt</code> file, encrypted in your
            browser before it leaves the machine, and you get a share link. Anything under
            10&nbsp;KB renders straight into the page for the reader, with a copy button.
            Larger snippets show the first 50 lines and expand on request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="db-h2">Why not just paste it in chat</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Chat apps wrap long lines, eat indentation, and truncate walls of output.</li>
            <li>A link expires; a chat message sits in someone's history forever.</li>
            <li>The content is encrypted in your browser — the server stores bytes it cannot read.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="db-h2">Typical uses</h2>
        <p>
            Error logs and stack traces, a config file someone needs to copy verbatim,
            meeting notes, a long URL list, or any text that is too big for a message box
            and too small to deserve a document.
        </p>
    </Body>
</ToolsLanding>
